# Visual Go/No-Go EEG

Worked example accompanying the eeg-bids-converter skill. One participant,
one run, shortened to keep the example small. Not real data.

## Overview

Demonstrates a spec-valid single-subject BIDS-EEG dataset. 64-channel EEG
plus 1 EOG channel, sampled at 500 Hz, one participant, one run, ~10 s
duration (shortened from the source recording for this example). Task:
visual Go/No-Go.

### Experimental design

Independent variable: stimulus type (Go = blue square, No-Go = red
square). Dependent variables: button-press response and response time. No
control variables varied across trials.

## Dataset contents and structure

Standard BIDS layout only — no `derivatives/`, no `sourcedata/`, no
non-standard files.

## Methods

### Participants and recruitment

One participant (`sub-01`), no exclusions. See `participants.tsv` for
demographics, `participants.json` for column definitions.

### Acquisition

TMSi Refa 72-channel amplifier, linked-earlobes reference. Full parameters
in `sub-01_task-gonogo_eeg.json`.

### Task and paradigm

Participants pressed the space bar for Go stimuli (blue square) and
withheld the response for No-Go stimuli (red square). Single block, no
counter-balancing beyond stimulus order. See
`sub-01_task-gonogo_events.tsv` for trial-by-trial timing.

## Known issues, quality, and missing data

Channel T7 was noisy throughout and is marked `bad` in `channels.tsv`.
`EEGGround` was not stated in the source documentation and is recorded as
`"n/a"` rather than guessed.

## References and citation

Source archive: https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.0000000. Converted with the
eeg-bids-converter skill.

